From 99ecc34dfa3070879dcce1baeeab93f9d9924086 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Li <lizhi.xmu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:15:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deps: materialise full source trees (sparse patterns missed
 sub-directories)

The recipes cloned with `--sparse` and then `sparse-checkout set --no-cone /* !tests`.
In gitignore syntax `/*` matches top-level entries only, so sub-directories were never
checked out. nghttp3's CMakeLists sets CMAKE_MODULE_PATH to <src>/cmake and then does
include(Version) -> 'include could not find requested file: Version' -> configure fails.
Upstream does not hit this because their cached build tree skips configure entirely.
Affected recipes now materialise the full tree. The three intentionally narrow recipes
(angle-headers, amf, ...) are untouched.
---
 packages/avisynth-headers.cmake | 2 +-
 packages/brotli.cmake           | 2 +-
 packages/curl.cmake             | 2 +-
 packages/expat.cmake            | 2 +-
 packages/ffmpeg.cmake           | 2 +-
